# THE ORACLE PINS — the ONE place that names which legend-engine / legend-pure
# release is the spec (docs/UPSTREAM_BOUNDARY_PROGRAM.md §3 A: one release).
#
# Read by:
#   * .github/actions/gate-env      — CI clones exactly these commits (shallow, by SHA)
#   * tools/oracle-roots.sh         — the local gate scripts FAIL if the checkout at
#                                     LEGEND_ENGINE_ROOT / LEGEND_PURE_ROOT sits on a
#                                     different commit (every "phantom regression" in
#                                     docs/GATES.md was a stale or divergent checkout)
#   * tools/version-report.sh       — asserts every OTHER version identity in the
#                                     repo (root pom.xml's legend.engine.version /
#                                     legend.pure.version, tools/engine-runner, the
#                                     fixture snapshot) equals THIS release; `--check`
#                                     runs in CI beside oracle_roots_check
#
# THE RULE: the source checkouts pin a RELEASE TAG, never an arbitrary commit.
# Jars exist only at release tags, so a non-tag source pin makes an identical
# oracle jar impossible and the parser differential (gate 8) has to hand-
# adjudicate every construct on either side of the divergence
# (docs/version-skew-claims.tsv was 25 rows of that rent at 4.137.0+36).
#
#   LEGEND_ENGINE_RELEASE   the release; the jar version every upstream-facing
#                           pom resolves (pom.xml <legend.engine.version> must
#                           equal it — version-report.sh --check enforces)
#   LEGEND_PURE_RELEASE     DERIVED: the <legend.pure.version> that engine
#                           release's own pom declares (INV-1) — nobody types
#                           a pure version independently
#   *_SHA                   the COMMIT the tag points to (the tag object itself
#                           is a different SHA — CI and oracle_roots_check
#                           compare against HEAD, which is the commit)
#   *_DESCRIBE              the tag name, == legend-<repo>-<RELEASE> exactly
#
# Bumping = change LEGEND_ENGINE_RELEASE, derive LEGEND_PURE_RELEASE from the
# release's pom on Maven Central, resolve the two tag commits, move the local
# checkouts, then docs/UPSTREAM_BOUNDARY_HOMEWORK_2026_09_10.md §5 phases 2-6
# (regenerate, run tools/allgates.sh once, re-pin every moved row with a
# reason). Jar pins may only name what Central has published: tags and
# Central disagree (4.142.0 is tagged and unpublished).
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE, no quotes, no expansion — sourced by bash and parsed by CI.
LEGEND_ENGINE_RELEASE=4.138.2
LEGEND_PURE_RELEASE=5.92.0
LEGEND_ENGINE_REPO=finos/legend-engine
LEGEND_ENGINE_SHA=28e75114f6ed4e22ec23e19184aa7e95da81c7af
LEGEND_ENGINE_DESCRIBE=legend-engine-4.138.2
LEGEND_PURE_REPO=finos/legend-pure
LEGEND_PURE_SHA=b2ef7e832bc94a09985064fa4f341e5411aa5682
LEGEND_PURE_DESCRIBE=legend-pure-5.92.0
